# Automation orchestrator terminology

Red Hat styles the product name with only **Automation** capitalized. The second word is **orchestrator** (lowercase), not title case.

## Use in new prose

| Wrong | Correct |
|-------|---------|
| Automation Orchestrator | **Automation orchestrator** |
| automation orchestrator | **Automation orchestrator** |
| Ansible Automation Orchestrator (unless quoting docs literally) | **Automation orchestrator** |

**Abbreviation:** After first use, **Automation orchestrator (AO)** is fine; then **AO** alone in the same section.

**Headings:** Use sentence-style headings, for example `### Automation orchestrator` or `## Decision framework: when to add Automation orchestrator`, not `### Automation Orchestrator`.

Apply the same pattern in tables, callouts, catalog cards, hub copy, and maturity chips.

## When title case is OK

Keep **Orchestrator** capitalized only when matching an **external** artifact readers will see unchanged:

- Official document titles or KB headings (literal quotes)
- UI labels or screenshots that show title case
- Third-party quotes

Do not propagate title case into paraphrased guide prose.

